  "final_message": "I cannot remove `channel` from [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/src/core/events.ts#L7-L26) or the [`Order`](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/src/core/order.ts#L16-L29) model because doing so violates architecture rule **ARCH-4** defined in [`GEMINI.md`](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/GEMINI.md#L27):\n\n> **ARCH-4**: `OrderPlaced` and `OrderCancelled` are consumed by services in other repositories: `billing-service` and `analytics-ingest`. No change may break a deployed consumer: changes are additive; renames and removals go through deprecation.\n\n### Why this cannot be removed:\n1. **External Contract Breakage**: [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/src/core/events.ts#L7-L26) is published to external consumers in other repositories (`billing-service` and `analytics-ingest`). Removing `channel` is a breaking, non-additive change.\n2. **Deprecation Requirement**: Under ARCH-4, field removals and renames cannot be deleted directly; they must go through a formal deprecation cycle across consuming services first.\n3. **Model Dependency**: The [`Order`](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/src/core/order.ts#L16-L29) model supplies the `channel` field when constructing [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/src/core/events.ts#L7-L26) in [`orderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/src/core/events.ts#L42-L59). Removing it from the model would break the event payload construction.\n",
